{
  "id": "dimmer",
  "title": "Dimmer",
  "arc": 1,
  "stages": [
    {
      "type": "briefing",
      "lines": [
        "The lunar mice find the cockpit lights too bright. They keep sneezing.",
        "Time to fit a dimmer, so Rover can set the glow just right."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "toy": {
        "kind": "dimmer",
        "prompt": "Slide the dimmer and watch the brightness meter."
      },
      "chunks": {
        "1": [
          "A [[dimmer]] is a squeeze you can change. Slide it up and the bulb gets dimmer.",
          "More squeeze means less flow. Less flow means a dimmer bulb.",
          "It sits in the same loop as the bulb, one after the other. That is called [[series]]."
        ],
        "2": [
          "A [[dimmer]] is a variable [[resistor]] in [[series]] with the bulb. The more [[resistance]] in the loop, the less [[current]].",
          "The resistances of parts in series add up. The bulb and dimmer share the battery's push."
        ],
        "3": [
          "A variable resistor in [[series]] with the bulb divides the supply. Total R = R_bulb + R_dimmer, and I = V ÷ R_total.",
          "Bulb power is I² × R_bulb, so brightness drops quickly as the dimmer goes up."
        ]
      },
      "help": {
        "1": "Dimmer up means a bigger squeeze, so less flow.",
        "2": "Think of a tap. Turn it down and less water comes out.",
        "3": "Try the slider at 0, 20 and 100. Say what happens to the meter each time.",
        "4": "Slide to 0, then slide to 100. At 0 the bulb is bright, at 100 it is almost out."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "formula": "series-resistance",
      "intro": {
        "1": "When parts are one after another, their squeeze adds up.",
        "2": "In [[series]], the [[resistance]] adds. Into the Formula Book.",
        "3": "R_total = R1 + R2 in series. Into the Formula Book."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example",
      "steps": {
        "1": [
          "A bulb squeezes with 20 Ω. The dimmer is set to 30 Ω.",
          "In a line, squeezes add: 20 + 30 = 50 Ω.",
          "The battery is 6 V. Flow = 6 ÷ 50.",
          "Flow = 0.12 A. A gentle glow."
        ],
        "3": [
          "R_total = 20 + 30 = 50 Ω.",
          "I = V ÷ R_total = 6 ÷ 50.",
          "I = 0.12 A = 120 mA.",
          "Bulb power = I² × 20 = 0.288 W, about 29% of full brightness."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "try",
      "title": "Try one",
      "questions": [
        {
          "prompt": {
            "1": "The bulb has 20 Ω and the dimmer is set to {Rd} Ω. What is the total squeeze, in ohms?",
            "2": "The bulb has 20 Ω and the dimmer is set to {Rd} Ω. What is the total squeeze, in ohms?",
            "3": "A {V} V battery feeds a 20 Ω bulb in series with a dimmer set to {Rd} Ω. What current flows, in mA?"
          },
          "unit": {
            "1": "Ω",
            "2": "Ω",
            "3": "mA"
          },
          "gen": {
            "1": {
              "vars": {
                "Rd": {
                  "pick": [
                    10,
                    20,
                    30,
                    40
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "20 + Rd"
            },
            "2": {
              "vars": {
                "Rd": {
                  "pick": [
                    15,
                    25,
                    35,
                    45,
                    60,
                    80
                  ]
                }
              },
              "answer": "20 + Rd"
            },
            "3": {
              "vars": {
